1
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:26,840
Aiming for the spring sun
floating on the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:34,000
I kicked a pebble and my shoe flew off too.

3
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:42,100
Onto the head of the
piggy bank I'd been saving,

4
00:00:42,100 --> 00:00:48,440
they laughed, saying I'm still just a kid.

5
00:00:48,440 --> 00:00:55,280
Even if I stir up some energy somewhere,

6
00:00:55,280 --> 00:01:02,560
the yawn-inducing,
unchanging streets feel strangely kind.

7
00:01:03,740 --> 00:01:16,800
From the pointed-hat water tower,
the sunset falls toward the street corner.

8
00:01:20,940 --> 00:01:25,240
Tomorrow too, it'll end just like this

9
00:01:25,240 --> 00:01:29,060
Katsushika, Shibamata,
happiness again, they say.

10
00:01:29,060 --> 00:01:31,780
I only realized it after losing it.

11
00:01:31,780 --> 00:01:33,840
Because I'm such a fool.

12
00:01:42,160 --> 00:01:43,480
Look at this rare thing.

13
00:01:43,480 --> 00:01:44,960
A recorder

14
00:01:44,960 --> 00:01:46,940
Nowadays we call it a recorder.

15
00:01:49,520 --> 00:01:53,500
Back in the day, we'd use these for sword fights
or copy the charumera horn of the noodle vendors.

16
00:01:55,920 --> 00:01:57,140
You kids did too, right?

17
00:01:58,540 --> 00:02:00,920
When I was a kid, I played the flute.

18
00:02:01,460 --> 00:02:03,320
The flute is a transverse flute, right?

19
00:02:03,660 --> 00:02:05,920
Back then I was a Fuefuki Doji,
blowing on the golden tsuke.

20
00:02:06,460 --> 00:02:10,380
Sorry, that's a bit too
old for us to keep up with.

21
00:02:10,720 --> 00:02:12,080
I see. Never mind.

22
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:15,280
So, Reiko,
why were you learning something like that?

23
00:02:15,280 --> 00:02:20,320
Why? Because the first wind instrument
I ever picked up was the flute.

24
00:02:20,320 --> 00:02:23,240
Now that you mention it,
I started on the flute too.

25
00:02:23,880 --> 00:02:25,680
Mine was custom-made, in pure silver.

26
00:02:26,420 --> 00:02:30,040
Why do you two always have
to go for the classy stuff?

27
00:02:30,040 --> 00:02:34,360
Elementary school means recorders all over the country,
doesn't it?

28
00:02:34,360 --> 00:02:35,960
Well, if you say so.

29
00:02:36,780 --> 00:02:39,060
You must be really attached to it, Senpai.

30
00:02:39,060 --> 00:02:42,840
It's a shame we can't talk about
our nostalgic recorders together.

31
00:02:42,840 --> 00:02:44,020
That's not nothing, you know.

32
00:02:45,280 --> 00:02:46,620
It has initials engraved on it.

33
00:02:47,300 --> 00:02:49,120
Oh, it does.

34
00:02:49,680 --> 00:02:51,380
Could those be the initials of the owner?

35
00:02:51,780 --> 00:02:52,420
Probably.

36
00:02:59,080 --> 00:03:00,620
What's wrong, Ryo-chan?

37
00:03:01,100 --> 00:03:02,500
No, I just remembered something.

38
00:03:03,180 --> 00:03:06,040
Back then,
I once carved initials into one too.

39
00:03:06,700 --> 00:03:08,740
So it's a memory of your flute, Senpai.

40
00:03:08,740 --> 00:03:10,040
Do tell us.

41
00:03:10,040 --> 00:03:11,220
I want to hear it too.

42
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:15,920
Let me see,
it was back in fifth grade, I think.

43
00:03:22,200 --> 00:03:25,180
A girl named Himeno
transferred into our class.

44
00:03:26,140 --> 00:03:28,240
"I'm Yukiko Himeno. Nice to meet you."

45
00:03:28,900 --> 00:03:30,820
That girl was incredibly cute.

46
00:03:30,820 --> 00:03:32,940
She was basically the class idol.

47
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:35,820
Then one day, after some time had passed,

48
00:03:35,820 --> 00:03:37,920
she came over to me.

49
00:03:38,820 --> 00:03:40,370
Kankichi-kun,

50
00:03:40,420 --> 00:03:43,300
I have a little favor to ask you.

51
00:03:44,060 --> 00:03:44,820
Me?

52
00:03:47,480 --> 00:03:50,040
The class beauty wants
a favor from Kankichi?

53
00:03:50,700 --> 00:03:51,740
What's going on here?

54
00:03:52,760 --> 00:03:54,500
What is it, Himeno?
You want something from me?

55
00:03:55,200 --> 00:03:56,840
Well, that's

56
00:03:57,200 --> 00:03:58,960
What is it? Spit it out.

57
00:03:59,740 --> 00:04:00,640
N-no way...

58
00:04:02,720 --> 00:04:05,680
Kankichi, go out with me! Go out with me!

59
00:04:07,160 --> 00:04:08,380
Boy. This is trouble.

60
00:04:08,940 --> 00:04:10,680
It's actually about the flute.

61
00:04:11,080 --> 00:04:12,160
The flute?

62
00:04:12,380 --> 00:04:15,000
Yes, the vertical flute
we use in music class.

63
00:04:15,300 --> 00:04:17,000
What's wrong with the flute?

64
00:04:17,300 --> 00:04:18,535
A boy in my class

65
00:04:18,585 --> 00:04:22,440
seems to be swapping his flute
with mine without me noticing.

66
00:04:22,620 --> 00:04:23,140
What?

67
00:04:23,900 --> 00:04:27,860
Every time I check, it's different.
So I've already switched to five new ones.

68
00:04:29,260 --> 00:04:32,640
I see, so he swaps Himeno's
flute and gets an indirect kiss

69
00:04:32,640 --> 00:04:34,440
It's just creeping me out.

70
00:04:35,220 --> 00:04:38,220
I thought Kankichi-kun might be
able to do something about it.

71
00:04:39,160 --> 00:04:39,640
Himeno

72
00:04:39,640 --> 00:04:41,700
Okay, don't cry.

73
00:04:41,700 --> 00:04:43,320
Leave it to me, I'll take care of it.

74
00:04:44,080 --> 00:04:44,400
Really?

75
00:04:45,440 --> 00:04:46,860
Yeah, just leave it to me.

76
00:04:50,980 --> 00:04:52,840
Listen, until music class,

77
00:04:52,840 --> 00:04:55,580
I'll leave my flute in Himeno's flute case.

78
00:04:55,580 --> 00:04:56,760
Wait.

79
00:04:57,960 --> 00:04:59,460
You'll be able to tell
who swapped them, right?

80
00:05:00,380 --> 00:05:02,080
No, that's disgusting.

81
00:05:02,080 --> 00:05:03,600
That's a bit too much, isn't it?

82
00:05:04,100 --> 00:05:06,860
Right away, the bait was taken
and the flutes had been swapped.

83
00:05:07,700 --> 00:05:09,640
So I carved the K again and left it there.

84
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:12,020
It's been swapped again.

85
00:05:12,500 --> 00:05:13,820
After two or three months,

86
00:05:13,820 --> 00:05:15,300
most of the boys in the class

87
00:05:15,300 --> 00:05:18,460
are blowing flutes with
the K mark I carved on them.

88
00:05:20,040 --> 00:05:21,980
Aren't you ashamed of yourselves?

89
00:05:22,700 --> 00:05:25,240
Secretly swapping Himeno's
flute for your own.

90
00:05:25,240 --> 00:05:28,740
Because the evidence is
the K mark on your flutes.

91
00:05:28,740 --> 00:05:30,220
It's true!

92
00:05:31,360 --> 00:05:35,280
This is the mark from my flute
that I left in place of Himeno's.

93
00:05:35,280 --> 00:05:37,240
So you came too!

94
00:05:40,960 --> 00:05:44,780
Serves them right!
They won't do that again, I bet.

95
00:05:45,180 --> 00:05:46,600
Thanks, Kankichi.

96
00:05:48,200 --> 00:05:51,440
So the case was solved
without a hitch, though.

97
00:05:51,440 --> 00:05:52,660
I see.

98
00:05:52,660 --> 00:05:53,860
That's good.

99
00:05:55,780 --> 00:05:56,140
Honestly.

100
00:05:56,540 --> 00:05:58,380
Hey, hasn't a lost item been turned in?

101
00:05:58,380 --> 00:05:59,680
Lost item.

102
00:06:00,820 --> 00:06:01,920
That's right.

103
00:06:02,420 --> 00:06:04,000
What's this? Is it Junpei's?

104
00:06:05,040 --> 00:06:07,720
Yeah, it says
"J" for Junpei right here, see?

105
00:06:07,720 --> 00:06:09,260
There's no doubt about it, it's mine.

106
00:06:09,260 --> 00:06:12,560
That's good.
Make sure you don't drop it this time.

107
00:06:13,040 --> 00:06:14,000
Yeah, thanks a lot.

108
00:06:15,120 --> 00:06:16,000
Well then.

109
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:18,260
Senpai, it's time for patrol!

110
00:06:18,260 --> 00:06:21,320
Even if I don't look like it,
I've got a lot on my plate, you know.

111
00:06:21,320 --> 00:06:24,820
I have to keep up with what's happening in society,
after all.

112
00:06:34,520 --> 00:06:36,260
Nakagawa! I'll go after all!

113
00:06:36,380 --> 00:06:37,180
Senpai!

114
00:06:37,700 --> 00:06:40,400
Honestly, Ryo-chan, you're so fickle!

115
00:06:52,180 --> 00:06:53,780
It has gotten old, hasn't it.

116
00:06:59,240 --> 00:06:59,600
Whoa!

117
00:06:59,720 --> 00:07:00,120
Eek!

118
00:07:00,200 --> 00:07:01,380
Th-that no, no!

119
00:07:01,860 --> 00:07:02,760
Ah!

120
00:07:03,160 --> 00:07:03,760
Idiot!

121
00:07:04,320 --> 00:07:06,080
Gotcha, Kankichi!

122
00:07:06,660 --> 00:07:08,820
What, it's Tonpei and Chin-kichi!

123
00:07:09,060 --> 00:07:10,320
You guys came too?

124
00:07:10,580 --> 00:07:12,020
Saw it in the paper this morning.

125
00:07:12,120 --> 00:07:15,200
Figured I'd take one more
look before they tear it down.

126
00:07:16,020 --> 00:07:16,720
Me too.

127
00:07:22,440 --> 00:07:23,620
Ha

128
00:07:23,860 --> 00:07:27,200
Earlier, I got yelled at all of a sudden,
and my body just reacted on instinct.

129
00:07:27,200 --> 00:07:29,500
That thrill feels nostalgic now, doesn't it?

130
00:07:29,500 --> 00:07:30,560
Totally.

131
00:07:31,700 --> 00:07:33,480
Our classroom was right here.

132
00:07:35,040 --> 00:07:36,240
Such tiny desks.

133
00:07:36,240 --> 00:07:38,380
We're the ones who got bigger.

134
00:07:38,380 --> 00:07:40,220
What, only ten kids per class?

135
00:07:40,600 --> 00:07:42,040
Urban depopulation

136
00:07:42,040 --> 00:07:44,880
Back in our day,
there were nearly fifty of us.

137
00:07:45,240 --> 00:07:50,580
With so many of us, we could sneak into the next
class and eat lunch without anyone noticing, right?

138
00:07:51,400 --> 00:07:52,460
Yeah, we did that!

139
00:07:52,460 --> 00:07:54,620
Because the school lunches always ran short,

140
00:07:54,620 --> 00:07:56,860
didn't it become one of
the school's seven mysteries?

141
00:07:59,180 --> 00:08:00,800
Speaking of the Seven Mysteries,
there's that one

142
00:08:01,320 --> 00:08:04,120
where a ghost appears in
the big hallway mirror.

143
00:08:06,420 --> 00:08:08,180
But the real culprit was

144
00:08:08,180 --> 00:08:09,540
Kankichi!

145
00:08:09,540 --> 00:08:10,760
Yep, we did that!

146
00:08:10,760 --> 00:08:12,080
And then there's that one

147
00:08:12,080 --> 00:08:15,300
where Beethoven's eyes
move in the music room.

148
00:08:17,180 --> 00:08:18,820
That one was Kankichi too.

149
00:08:19,240 --> 00:08:21,160
He was peeking out from behind the wall,
wasn't he?

150
00:08:21,160 --> 00:08:24,000
He usually covered it up by sticking
marbles in the eye holes, right?

151
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:27,580
We pretty much made up the
school's Seven Mysteries ourselves.

152
00:08:29,740 --> 00:08:33,820
Right, and speaking of the music room, we also pulled
off the one where the piano plays by itself, remember?

153
00:08:33,820 --> 00:08:36,640
Oh yeah, that's right!

154
00:08:41,860 --> 00:08:42,980
Will this do?

155
00:08:43,360 --> 00:08:45,160
Looks like there's really no one here.

156
00:08:45,920 --> 00:08:47,660
Hey, someone's coming!

157
00:08:47,660 --> 00:08:48,360
Okay.

158
00:09:07,040 --> 00:09:07,840
Yoji!

159
00:09:14,360 --> 00:09:16,380
Tonbei-kun and Chin-kichi-kun!

160
00:09:17,880 --> 00:09:20,338
So it was you playing the piano,

161
00:09:20,388 --> 00:09:22,180
Kan-kichi-kun, just as I thought.

162
00:09:22,400 --> 00:09:22,980
Busted.

163
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:27,260
Even ghosts can't scare
anyone with nonsense like that.

164
00:09:29,240 --> 00:09:29,980
How about this?

165
00:09:38,160 --> 00:09:39,100
Wow.

166
00:09:42,100 --> 00:09:43,820
You're really good, Himeno.

167
00:09:43,820 --> 00:09:45,580
I love playing the piano.

168
00:09:45,580 --> 00:09:47,640
My dream is to become a pianist.

169
00:09:56,680 --> 00:09:57,960
Himeno, are you ready?

170
00:09:58,000 --> 00:09:58,420
Yeah, I'm ready.

171
00:09:59,400 --> 00:09:59,740
Okay.

172
00:10:08,940 --> 00:10:10,400
Weird, at this hour.

173
00:10:20,560 --> 00:10:21,740
Blind spot.

174
00:10:21,740 --> 00:10:22,840
Aaaaaah!

175
00:10:23,720 --> 00:10:24,880
Uraaameshiya!

176
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:28,560
Uraaameshiya!

177
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:34,100
Hey, Kankichi! You lot again!

178
00:10:34,240 --> 00:10:34,880
Run!

179
00:10:37,340 --> 00:10:37,940
Himeno!

180
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:41,220
Hey! Wait!

181
00:10:51,740 --> 00:10:59,300
Himeno went to Europe to study piano right after elementary school, didn't she?
What's she doing now?

182
00:11:01,900 --> 00:11:02,960
You don't know?

183
00:11:04,720 --> 00:11:08,420
Himeno died.
In a traffic accident last year.

184
00:11:09,800 --> 00:11:13,980
She made her dream come true and became a pianist,
and she was working hard at it.

185
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:17,920
I see. I didn't know.

186
00:11:20,080 --> 00:11:20,800
Motokichi!

187
00:11:29,300 --> 00:11:31,320
Hey, can't you hear piano music?

188
00:11:37,820 --> 00:11:39,240
I can hear it, actually.

189
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:40,860
There's supposed to be no one here, right?

190
00:11:41,430 --> 00:11:42,960
No way...

191
00:11:52,420 --> 00:11:54,200
It's coming from up ahead, isn't it?

192
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:56,080
Let's go check it out.

193
00:12:00,980 --> 00:12:02,580
It's just the after-school chime.

194
00:12:02,580 --> 00:12:04,880
So it rings automatically now

195
00:12:05,840 --> 00:12:06,800
Alright, let's go.

196
00:12:08,320 --> 00:12:09,660
Are we going to the music room?

197
00:12:09,660 --> 00:12:11,220
That's the only place with a piano,
isn't it?

198
00:12:20,260 --> 00:12:21,560
Just as I thought, it's coming from here.

199
00:12:22,020 --> 00:12:24,280
Chinkichi, why don't you open the door?

200
00:12:24,280 --> 00:12:25,040
Me?

201
00:12:25,040 --> 00:12:26,760
Tonbe, you do it.

202
00:12:26,760 --> 00:12:28,180
Why does it have to be me?

203
00:12:28,180 --> 00:12:29,600
Kankichi, you open it.

204
00:12:29,600 --> 00:12:30,840
Fine, what a pain.

205
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:33,180
Then let's all three open it together.

206
00:12:34,060 --> 00:12:34,920
Here we go.

207
00:12:40,380 --> 00:12:42,180
A schoolkid's playing it!

208
00:12:43,120 --> 00:12:43,500
What?

209
00:12:43,500 --> 00:12:43,660
What the...?

210
00:12:47,440 --> 00:12:48,020
Himeno!

211
00:12:49,300 --> 00:12:50,340
I'm sorry!

212
00:12:51,520 --> 00:12:54,100
I'm sorry for using the
piano without permission...

213
00:12:55,920 --> 00:12:57,160
Who are you?

214
00:13:00,420 --> 00:13:02,740
So you're Himeno's daughter?

215
00:13:02,920 --> 00:13:04,660
No wonder you look just like her.

216
00:13:04,660 --> 00:13:06,060
My name's Megumi.

217
00:13:06,460 --> 00:13:09,700
Aren't you by any chance
the Tonchikkan trio?

218
00:13:10,420 --> 00:13:12,340
How do you know that?

219
00:13:13,500 --> 00:13:14,680
I heard a lot about it,

220
00:13:15,040 --> 00:13:16,840
Himeno would tell us

221
00:13:17,820 --> 00:13:20,020
just as I imagined you'd be.

222
00:13:20,020 --> 00:13:20,880
All three of you,

223
00:13:21,400 --> 00:13:22,400
painted the statue gold

224
00:13:22,400 --> 00:13:25,280
and turned Ninomiya Kinjiro into
"Golden Kinjiro."

225
00:13:25,960 --> 00:13:27,660
Using an alcohol lamp from the science lab,

226
00:13:27,660 --> 00:13:29,420
you grilled dried squid and ate it.

227
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:32,140
Mom said her elementary school days

228
00:13:32,140 --> 00:13:33,300
were the most fun of her life.

229
00:13:33,300 --> 00:13:34,740
She talked about them often.

230
00:13:35,120 --> 00:13:37,480
This morning, the newspaper reported

231
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:38,720
that the school is going to be torn down,

232
00:13:39,120 --> 00:13:40,740
so I wanted to take one last look.

233
00:13:42,040 --> 00:13:45,440
So when we came to the music room and saw the piano,
I just couldn't help myself.

234
00:13:45,440 --> 00:13:48,700
And then we happened to walk in on you?

235
00:13:48,700 --> 00:13:51,000
Feels like fate, somehow.

236
00:13:51,360 --> 00:13:53,260
Megumi, you're good at the piano too,

237
00:13:53,260 --> 00:13:56,680
so is your dream to become
a pianist like your mom?

238
00:13:57,340 --> 00:13:57,700
Yes.

239
00:13:58,760 --> 00:14:01,360
But I'm not confident I can be like Mom.

240
00:14:01,800 --> 00:14:03,300
Not confident?

241
00:14:03,300 --> 00:14:05,740
You were playing so well back there!

242
00:14:05,740 --> 00:14:07,760
Compared to Mom, I'm nowhere near

243
00:14:08,180 --> 00:14:10,200
I've always made Mom my goal.

244
00:14:10,860 --> 00:14:12,740
But she's gone now too,

245
00:14:13,180 --> 00:14:16,820
and I keep thinking that when Mom was playing,
she must have been even better.

246
00:14:17,420 --> 00:14:18,500
That's not true.

247
00:14:18,500 --> 00:14:21,320
When your mom was your age,

248
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:22,960
Mom was?

249
00:14:22,960 --> 00:14:23,560
Yeah.

250
00:14:25,560 --> 00:14:26,620
What's wrong?

251
00:14:26,620 --> 00:14:28,940
Remember, we buried a time capsule,

252
00:14:28,940 --> 00:14:30,620
a time capsule.

253
00:14:30,620 --> 00:14:33,220
Come to think of it, when we graduated,
we buried it in the schoolyard.

254
00:14:33,220 --> 00:14:35,760
Right, Himeno's stuff is in there too,
isn't it?

255
00:14:36,820 --> 00:14:38,100
I'll match it up for you.

256
00:14:38,100 --> 00:14:40,220
Back when Megumi's mom was
about the same age as her.

257
00:14:41,500 --> 00:14:43,840
I'm sure it was around here, I think.

258
00:14:43,840 --> 00:14:46,100
It was over twenty years ago, after all.

259
00:14:46,920 --> 00:14:48,120
Hey, Ryo-san.

260
00:14:48,120 --> 00:14:51,960
Earlier, when I said I wasn't confident,

261
00:14:51,960 --> 00:14:54,200
you said Mom was the same way, didn't you?

262
00:14:54,960 --> 00:14:58,100
Would you tell me about those days?

263
00:14:59,460 --> 00:15:01,740
That was the year we graduated.

264
00:15:03,940 --> 00:15:05,220
Studying abroad?

265
00:15:05,420 --> 00:15:06,180
Yeah, that's right.

266
00:15:06,860 --> 00:15:07,740
You sure you'll be okay?

267
00:15:07,740 --> 00:15:10,080
If you go overseas,
nobody will understand Japanese,

268
00:15:10,740 --> 00:15:12,800
and you'll have to eat with
knives and forks instead, right?

269
00:15:13,600 --> 00:15:15,720
Are you worried about me?

270
00:15:15,800 --> 00:15:17,440
No, not really.

271
00:15:18,320 --> 00:15:20,900
I'll miss everyone at this school, though.

272
00:15:21,580 --> 00:15:22,520
I've already made up my mind.

273
00:15:23,120 --> 00:15:23,740
I see.

274
00:15:24,260 --> 00:15:26,280
Himeno is really good at piano,

275
00:15:26,280 --> 00:15:30,220
so obviously studying abroad
is better than staying in Japan.

276
00:15:30,920 --> 00:15:31,840
Kankichi-kun,

277
00:15:32,800 --> 00:15:34,280
good luck. We're rooting for you.

278
00:15:34,280 --> 00:15:36,820
But first I have to take an exam.

279
00:15:37,520 --> 00:15:39,340
Himeno, you're definitely going to pass.

280
00:15:40,740 --> 00:15:43,920
People from every school come to take it,
and they're all really good.

281
00:15:44,980 --> 00:15:47,500
Don't worry, I guarantee you'll be fine.

282
00:15:49,360 --> 00:15:50,620
Thanks, Kankichi.

283
00:16:05,100 --> 00:16:07,760
No, I just can't play it
properly no matter what.

284
00:16:07,760 --> 00:16:11,320
Yes. There's only one
week left until the test.

285
00:16:12,100 --> 00:16:15,860
What's wrong? Just the other day
you were playing so beautifully.

286
00:16:20,120 --> 00:16:22,084
It's no good.

287
00:16:22,134 --> 00:16:25,660
I can't think of a good
way to get my hands to do it.

288
00:16:26,020 --> 00:16:26,560
Well then, see you.

289
00:16:26,780 --> 00:16:27,480
See you tomorrow.

290
00:16:30,060 --> 00:16:30,874
Mr. Nagashima,

291
00:16:30,924 --> 00:16:35,820
your hit in your 36th at-bat turned into
a walk-off grand slam to win the game,

292
00:16:37,760 --> 00:16:38,640
I wonder what that was about?

293
00:16:39,140 --> 00:16:39,500
Yes.

294
00:16:39,500 --> 00:16:41,720
Until now I had been putting
too much force into it,

295
00:16:41,720 --> 00:16:44,060
and the bat wouldn't swing smoothly.

296
00:16:44,420 --> 00:16:45,720
So I swung with all my might and missed,

297
00:16:45,720 --> 00:16:46,940
and when I landed on my backside,

298
00:16:46,940 --> 00:16:48,780
all the tension suddenly left my shoulders.

299
00:16:49,140 --> 00:16:50,240
I was relaxed,

300
00:16:50,240 --> 00:16:52,020
and swinging the bat without tensing up

301
00:16:52,020 --> 00:16:53,020
must have been what worked.

302
00:16:53,740 --> 00:16:54,660
Yeah, this is it.

303
00:16:57,520 --> 00:16:58,720
Nice

304
00:16:59,220 --> 00:17:00,520
Making that serious face,

305
00:17:00,520 --> 00:17:01,740
you don't need to copy the sheet music.

306
00:17:01,740 --> 00:17:04,000
There's an easier way.

307
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:04,720
What is it?

308
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:06,980
Just do this.

309
00:17:07,760 --> 00:17:07,900
See?

310
00:17:10,960 --> 00:17:12,720
See, your shoulders relaxed!

311
00:17:15,180 --> 00:17:16,160
Don't interrupt me!

312
00:17:17,460 --> 00:17:19,060
Hey, wait, Himeno!

313
00:17:22,180 --> 00:17:24,060
That was a huge blunder.

314
00:17:24,580 --> 00:17:26,040
Well, obviously!

315
00:17:26,320 --> 00:17:29,200
Shut up!
I thought it was a good idea at the time!

316
00:17:31,720 --> 00:17:35,123
After that, I tried all sorts
of things to help Himeno relax,

317
00:17:35,173 --> 00:17:36,900
but none of them really worked.

318
00:17:39,260 --> 00:17:40,160
No good.

319
00:17:41,380 --> 00:17:44,720
Himeno, don't look so tense.

320
00:17:44,720 --> 00:17:47,280
Loosen your shoulders and relax.

321
00:17:47,280 --> 00:17:49,320
I told you to stop interrupting.

322
00:17:49,320 --> 00:17:51,660
I hate you, Kankichi!

323
00:17:52,280 --> 00:17:54,380
Himeno, open up, will you?

324
00:17:54,380 --> 00:17:56,420
I can't climb up on my own.

325
00:17:57,900 --> 00:18:01,060
In the end, she wouldn't even speak to me.

326
00:18:13,720 --> 00:18:15,140
It's hopeless, no matter what I do.

327
00:18:15,720 --> 00:18:17,320
Playing like this,
there's no way I'll get in.

328
00:18:21,660 --> 00:18:22,700
Cheer up.

329
00:18:22,700 --> 00:18:24,480
You can do it.

330
00:18:27,100 --> 00:18:27,680
Himeno.

331
00:18:28,540 --> 00:18:28,960
That's right.

332
00:18:29,920 --> 00:18:31,580
You there, girl.

333
00:18:31,580 --> 00:18:33,580
What's troubling you?

334
00:18:35,640 --> 00:18:36,900
It's me, it's me!

335
00:18:37,760 --> 00:18:43,700
Can't you tell who's right in front of you?
Don't tell me you can't see. Look me in the eye!

336
00:18:45,260 --> 00:18:54,520
Got it? I'm not speaking bentō-ben, I'm speaking Tōhoku dialect.
I've been here listening to you play the whole time.

337
00:18:54,520 --> 00:18:59,200
And don't worry,
you have more than enough talent.

338
00:18:59,740 --> 00:19:07,520
Just relax your shoulders.
I know you really love the piano.

339
00:19:07,760 --> 00:19:11,120
You used to play with so much more joy,
didn't you?

340
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:16,360
If you relax and enjoy playing,
you'll surely get good results.

341
00:19:18,300 --> 00:19:19,780
Yes, Mr. Beethoven.

342
00:19:23,480 --> 00:19:25,840
Relax your shoulders and loosen up.

343
00:19:41,140 --> 00:19:42,580
That's it, keep it up.

344
00:19:43,680 --> 00:19:45,180
All of this up until now...

345
00:19:45,740 --> 00:19:48,380
you were doing all that just to help me relax,
weren't you?

346
00:19:49,400 --> 00:19:49,760
Thank you.

347
00:19:50,400 --> 00:19:51,200
Kankichi-kun.

348
00:20:18,140 --> 00:20:19,360
Congratulations!

349
00:20:19,360 --> 00:20:20,460
Congratulations!

350
00:20:20,460 --> 00:20:22,680
Congratulations!

351
00:20:22,680 --> 00:20:24,520
Way to go, Himeno!

352
00:20:24,520 --> 00:20:25,680
Congratulations!

353
00:20:27,220 --> 00:20:28,520
That's how it is.

354
00:20:28,520 --> 00:20:30,040
Mom, that really happened?

355
00:20:30,040 --> 00:20:32,460
Hey, did you find it?

356
00:20:32,460 --> 00:20:33,500
I give up.

357
00:20:33,500 --> 00:20:34,560
We can't find it.

358
00:20:35,320 --> 00:20:37,400
Where on earth did we bury it?

359
00:20:40,120 --> 00:20:41,300
Kankichi-kun!

360
00:20:43,580 --> 00:20:44,440
Himeno.

361
00:20:45,860 --> 00:20:47,320
Thank you, Mr. Beethoven.

362
00:20:47,320 --> 00:20:50,120
So you knew all along?

363
00:20:50,660 --> 00:20:54,160
Even when I go abroad,
I won't forget you, Kankichi-kun.

364
00:20:54,560 --> 00:20:57,360
Because you're my Beethoven, Kankichi-kun.

365
00:20:59,300 --> 00:21:00,040
Do your best, okay?

366
00:21:00,760 --> 00:21:01,120
Yeah.

367
00:21:06,260 --> 00:21:07,340
Did you find it?

368
00:21:07,760 --> 00:21:10,160
Kankichi! No, nothing at all!

369
00:21:10,340 --> 00:21:12,141
Did we really bury it?!

370
00:21:12,191 --> 00:21:14,380
Now this is getting suspicious!

371
00:21:14,720 --> 00:21:17,100
It's too dark to search any longer!

372
00:21:17,280 --> 00:21:17,720
But!

373
00:21:18,700 --> 00:21:21,520
But the demolition starts tomorrow!

374
00:21:21,920 --> 00:21:23,060
Ah...

375
00:21:23,060 --> 00:21:25,520
But it's so dark now, we can't...

376
00:21:25,520 --> 00:21:29,300
If it's really buried there,
we'll never get over it!

377
00:21:30,660 --> 00:21:32,040
Megumi-chan...

378
00:21:32,040 --> 00:21:35,660
Tonpe! Chinkichi! Turn on all
the lights in the school building!

379
00:21:38,020 --> 00:21:39,540
It's brighter than I thought.

380
00:21:39,540 --> 00:21:41,760
We're finding it tonight, no matter what!

381
00:21:42,440 --> 00:21:43,520
It has to be here somewhere.

382
00:21:43,520 --> 00:21:45,720
I'll dig up every single spot.

383
00:21:46,640 --> 00:21:48,340
Don't worry, Megumi.

384
00:21:48,340 --> 00:21:50,560
If anyone can find it, he will.

385
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:53,200
Chief, the demolition
schedule is going to change!

386
00:21:53,540 --> 00:21:54,260
I don't care!

387
00:21:54,260 --> 00:21:56,940
And you two,
don't you dare slack off either.

388
00:21:56,940 --> 00:21:59,740
Found it, here it is!

389
00:22:00,400 --> 00:22:01,280
Did you find it?

390
00:22:01,380 --> 00:22:02,340
No doubt about it.

391
00:22:04,520 --> 00:22:06,180
Himeno's is

392
00:22:08,380 --> 00:22:09,460
This is Mom's

393
00:22:09,460 --> 00:22:10,340
Hold it up and show us.

394
00:22:10,340 --> 00:22:13,900
Her mom should be in the sixth grade,
same as Megumi.

395
00:22:13,900 --> 00:22:14,520
Here.

396
00:22:14,520 --> 00:22:16,440
Hey, there's ours too!

397
00:22:16,440 --> 00:22:18,960
What did we write? I can't remember at all.

398
00:22:19,700 --> 00:22:22,380
"Future me: jet pilot."

399
00:22:22,380 --> 00:22:24,820
"Future me: Prime Minister."

400
00:22:24,820 --> 00:22:26,420
And a marble.

401
00:22:26,420 --> 00:22:29,620
What idiots, writing things like that.

402
00:22:29,620 --> 00:22:31,360
What, show us yours too, Kankichi!

403
00:22:31,360 --> 00:22:33,480
I'm not as childish as you lot.

404
00:22:34,240 --> 00:22:36,560
I'm the captain of the Earth Defense Force.

405
00:22:37,760 --> 00:22:42,480
That's the most childish one! There's a mud dumpling in here too. Yeah,
this one's Himeno's.

406
00:22:45,800 --> 00:22:49,980
To my future self:
are you active as a pianist?

407
00:22:50,860 --> 00:22:54,120
Have children all over the
world listened to your piano?

408
00:22:55,500 --> 00:23:01,680
If you've lost confidence or feel discouraged now,
remember me from these days.

409
00:23:01,680 --> 00:23:06,300
Please. No matter what happens,
I really love the piano!

410
00:23:07,960 --> 00:23:12,060
To my future self, Class 6-2, Yukiko Himeno.

411
00:23:14,400 --> 00:23:17,120
That brooch,
it's the one Himeno always wore.

412
00:23:17,120 --> 00:23:20,860
So Mom was just like me, too.

413
00:23:24,940 --> 00:23:27,780
Thank you all.
Thanks to you, I've made up my mind.

414
00:23:28,320 --> 00:23:30,820
I'll follow the path Mom walked.

415
00:23:31,580 --> 00:23:33,560
Because I love the piano too.

416
00:23:34,320 --> 00:23:36,560
I see. Himeno will be happy too.

417
00:23:38,240 --> 00:23:40,480
Well, I'll walk you home, Megumi.

418
00:23:40,480 --> 00:23:41,060
Yes.

419
00:23:43,700 --> 00:23:46,220
I'm really glad I came to this school today.

420
00:23:47,020 --> 00:23:48,100
Us too.

421
00:23:48,680 --> 00:23:50,820
I got to meet my old self again.

422
00:23:51,680 --> 00:23:53,480
The school building called us all here.

423
00:23:53,480 --> 00:23:56,340
It gave us one last memory to treasure.

424
00:24:16,940 --> 00:24:20,620
But there's a call coming in.

425
00:24:21,760 --> 00:24:27,420
If it's you, I wake up easily.

426
00:24:27,940 --> 00:24:31,820
Even boring stories,

427
00:24:31,820 --> 00:24:36,620
set my whole body on fire.

428
00:24:36,620 --> 00:24:43,240
But I want to see my friends.

429
00:24:43,240 --> 00:24:58,360
I surely want to be loved, melting together
so much it makes everyone a little jealous.

430
00:24:59,160 --> 00:25:02,200
I surely want to confide.

431
00:25:02,960 --> 00:25:07,980
Somehow, only love is out of tune.

432
00:25:08,940 --> 00:25:12,200
Even my bravado.

433
00:25:12,200 --> 00:25:15,860
Don't hide everything.

434
00:25:21,120 --> 00:25:21,980
This is bad!

435
00:25:22,300 --> 00:25:25,180
Higurashi, the psychic cop who
only wakes once every four years,

436
00:25:25,180 --> 00:25:28,000
we woke him before the Olympic year!

437
00:25:28,360 --> 00:25:30,180
He's a terrible sleeper.

438
00:25:30,180 --> 00:25:32,320
If he goes on a rampage
with his psychic powers,

439
00:25:32,320 --> 00:25:34,240
the whole town will be wrecked!

440
00:25:34,700 --> 00:25:37,140
It's still too early for the next Olympics.

441
00:25:37,480 --> 00:25:38,020
Nice to meet you.

